## Overview
#c1[overview,i5] Signer appends cryptographic signatures to bytes using secret keys and salts, while Serializer subclasses wrap signers to serialize arbitrary data structures into signed strings.
  > docs/concepts.rst:8-11 #8446375b6053
  > docs/concepts.rst:60-63 #8cb3ba5bc309
  > docs/serializer.rst:6-9 #0887e43dd873
  > docs/signer.rst:16 #7fcc7475b4f4
#c2[overview,i5] Secret keys can be supplied as an ordered list, enabling key rotation by signing with the newest key and validating across historical keys.
  > docs/concepts.rst:116-119 #343f8b7f541a
  > docs/serializer.rst:85-86 #ad005ffb454c
  > src/itsdangerous/serializer.py:208 #4ef723528107
  > src/itsdangerous/signer.py:139 #631f9f46207d
#c3[overview,i5] TimestampSigner and TimedSerializer record generation timestamps alongside payloads, allowing unsign operations to enforce expiration limits via max_age.
  > docs/timed.rst:6-8 #7742c3101efb
  > docs/timed.rst:8-9 #4ff9c5b49a9d
  > docs/timed.rst:19-22 #d4b5b9f5fa22
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py::TimestampSigner.sign #58138f9920de
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py::TimedSerializer #7aae72ea6cd9
#c4[overview,i5] URLSafeSerializer and URLSafeTimedSerializer mix in compact JSON serialization, optional zlib compression, and URL-safe base64 encoding to produce web-safe tokens.
  > docs/url_safe.rst:7-8 #89cc291f0098
  > src/itsdangerous/_json.py::_CompactJSON #9510131aae41
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializerMixin #1b2723627ade
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializerMixin.dump_payload #337cc17a522e
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializer #f82417cd241a
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeTimedSerializer #2ef0e70571b8
#c5[overview,i5] All exceptions derive from BadData, with BadSignature and BadPayload exposing failed payloads or underlying exceptions to aid debugging.
  > docs/exceptions.rst:1-22 #a5862d4c7c89
  > docs/serializer.rst:39-43 #bf9811e03d98
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::BadData #dd4e1e9667a0
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::BadSignature.__init__ #8c23f8689345
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::BadPayload #564bc548d3f2
#c6[overview,i5] Cryptographic verification ensures data round-tripping through untrusted client environments cannot be modified without knowledge of the secret key.
  > README.md::ItsDangerous #9862506eae8f
  > docs/index.rst:11-12 #e8afec3a3971
  > docs/index.rst:18-20 #61a539573aaa
  > docs/index.rst:45-47 #e67e612e02ac
  > docs/signer.rst:28-29 #a08adebe4972

## (root)
#c7[i5] ItsDangerous cryptographically signs data to ensure tokens passed to untrusted environments have not been tampered with.
  > README.md::ItsDangerous #9862506eae8f
#c8[i4] ItsDangerous allows customizing data serialization, compresses data as needed, and can automatically add and verify timestamps when loading tokens.
  > README.md::ItsDangerous #9862506eae8f
#c9[i3] Tokens can be generated and loaded using the URLSafeSerializer class with a secret key and salt.
  > README.md::"A Simple Example" #b1a9b67142d2
#c10[i2] The Pallets organization develops and supports ItsDangerous and accepts donations at palletsprojects.com/donate.
  > README.md::Donate #d5eca4501200

## docs
#c11[i3] The docs Makefile sets SPHINXBUILD to sphinx-build, SOURCEDIR to ., and BUILDDIR to _build by default.
  > docs/Makefile:6-8 #7a6c3999b76c
#c12[i4] The default target help runs SPHINXBUILD in make mode (-M help) using SOURCEDIR, BUILDDIR, SPHINXOPTS, and O.
  > docs/Makefile:11-12 #b30f15b65725
#c13[i4] The catch-all pattern target routes all unknown targets to SPHINXBUILD in make mode using target name $@.
  > docs/Makefile:18-19 #e66fb0e51be7
#c14[i2] The variable O functions as a shortcut for SPHINXOPTS when invoking build targets.
  > docs/Makefile:17 #b12166e9967f
#c15[i4] In docs/changes.rst, the Changes document includes content from ../CHANGES.rst using the include directive.
  > docs/changes.rst:4 #b0937da7f837
#c16[i4] ItsDangerous Signer signs bytes values, while Serializer wraps a signer to serialize and sign other data types.
  > docs/concepts.rst:8-11 #8446375b6053
#c17[i4] Changing the secret_key invalidates all existing tokens, which can be used to recover if an attacker discovers the key.
  > docs/concepts.rst:23 #bf56f58663ce
#c18[i4] The salt is combined with the secret key to distinguish contexts, and unlike the secret key, does not need to be private or random.
  > docs/concepts.rst:60-63 #8cb3ba5bc309
#c19[i3] Serializers using differing salts cannot load each other's dumped data and will raise BadSignature.
  > docs/concepts.rst:83-84 #b93dd6a16c99
#c20[i5] ItsDangerous accepts a list of secret keys ordered oldest to newest, signing with the newest key and validating from newest to oldest.
  > docs/concepts.rst:116-119 #343f8b7f541a
#c21[i4] The default HMAC digest method in ItsDangerous signers is hashlib.sha1.
  > docs/concepts.rst:141-142 #cbee4a331587
#c22[i3] Configuring a signer with hashlib.sha512 produces longer tokens that consume more space in cookies and URLs.
  > docs/concepts.rst:153-154 #75fd3d8eaf0a
#c23[i3] The documentation release and version are resolved dynamically for 'itsdangerous' using get_version from pallets_sphinx_themes.
  > docs/conf.py:9 #6c76fe2f2cf3
#c24[i3] Sphinx extensions configured include autodoc, extlinks, intersphinx, log_cabinet, and pallets_sphinx_themes.
  > docs/conf.py:14-20 #0b7d72641fca
#c25[i2] Autodoc is configured to document both class and __init__ docstrings in source order with type hints in descriptions and preserved defaults.
  > docs/conf.py:21-24 #c8f7578f51a4
#c26[i2] The documentation HTML output uses the 'flask' theme with index_sidebar_logo disabled and sourcelink hidden.
  > docs/conf.py:35-36 #62923d51e83e
#c27[i2] External link patterns are established for GitHub issues and pull requests under pallets/itsdangerous.
  > docs/conf.py:25-28 #5416bcefd8f3
#c28[i4] The docs/encoding.rst document covers the itsdangerous.encoding module.
  > docs/encoding.rst:1 #40b196ac3da0
#c29[i5] The module itsdangerous.exc defines the BadData, BadSignature, BadTimeSignature, SignatureExpired, BadHeader, and BadPayload exceptions.
  > docs/exceptions.rst:1-22 #a5862d4c7c89
#c30[i5] Data sent to untrusted environments must be cryptographically signed to detect changes and ensure nobody has tampered with it upon return.
  > docs/index.rst:11-12 #e8afec3a3971
#c31[i4] Receivers can view the data, but cannot modify it without knowing the secret signing key.
  > docs/index.rst:18-20 #61a539573aaa
#c32[i3] ItsDangerous can be installed and updated via pip using the command `pip install -U itsdangerous`.
  > docs/index.rst:30 #77ecf647ba56
