  > docs/index.rst:38-40 #cbba0e00cb61
#c34[i3] Storing signed objects in cookies avoids server-stored sessions and reduces database queries.
  > docs/index.rst:42-44 #adad5cdead64
#c35[i3] Signed data safely round-trips between server and client, enabling passing server-side state to a client and back.
  > docs/index.rst:45-47 #e67e612e02ac
#c36[i3] If not previously defined, docs/make.bat sets the SPHINXBUILD environment variable to sphinx-build.
  > docs/make.bat:7-9 #811d12550ff8
#c37[i3] docs/make.bat assigns SOURCEDIR to . and BUILDDIR to _build.
  > docs/make.bat:10-11 #311b35e6d4ac
#c38[i3] Invoking docs/make.bat without arguments redirects execution to the help label.
  > docs/make.bat:13 #b567965c9820
#c39[i4] If running SPHINXBUILD results in errorlevel 9009, docs/make.bat echoes installation instructions and exits with code 1.
  > docs/make.bat:16-26 #2319dbe439be
#c40[i5] docs/make.bat builds documentation by invoking SPHINXBUILD with -M, the first argument, SOURCEDIR, BUILDDIR, and SPHINXOPTS.
  > docs/make.bat:28 #3ad05fb7e182
#c41[i3] Under the help label, docs/make.bat executes SPHINXBUILD with -M help %SOURCEDIR% %BUILDDIR% %SPHINXOPTS%.
  > docs/make.bat:32 #08d3c05a6b2e
#c42[i5] The Serializer class provides a dumps/loads interface to serialize objects to strings and sign them, unlike Signer which only signs bytes.
  > docs/serializer.rst:6-9 #0887e43dd873
#c43[i4] By default, Serializer serializes data to JSON using Python's built-in json module, but the internal serializer can be customized by subclassing.
  > docs/serializer.rst:28-29 #61d44463d6d8
#c44[i3] When a signature check fails, BadSignature exceptions provide a payload attribute to inspect tampered data for debugging purposes.
  > docs/serializer.rst:39-43 #bf9811e03d98
#c45[i4] A list of fallback_signers can be provided to validate old signatures when unsigning with the current signer fails.
  > docs/serializer.rst:85-86 #ad005ffb454c
#c46[i5] The Signer class attaches a signature to a specific string, appending the signature separated by a dot.
  > docs/signer.rst:16 #7fcc7475b4f4
#c47[i5] The Signer.unsign method validates a signed string and retrieves the original value.
  > docs/signer.rst:16-17 #57acdb8db8ef
#c48[i3] If unicode strings are passed to the signer, they are implicitly encoded to UTF-8.
  > docs/signer.rst:24 #266254aac97a
#c49[i3] After unsigning, it is not possible to distinguish whether the original input was a unicode string or a bytestring.
  > docs/signer.rst:25-26 #46366a283467
#c50[i4] If a signed value is modified, the signature fails to match and unsigning raises a BadSignature exception.
  > docs/signer.rst:28-29 #a08adebe4972
#c51[i5] The TimestampSigner class enables expiring signatures by appending timestamp information and signing it.
  > docs/timed.rst:6-8 #7742c3101efb
#c52[i4] During unsigning with TimestampSigner, the timestamp can be validated to confirm it is not older than a specified maximum age.
  > docs/timed.rst:8-9 #4ff9c5b49a9d
#c53[i4] Passing max_age to TimestampSigner.unsign raises an itsdangerous.exc.SignatureExpired exception if the signature's age exceeds the limit.
  > docs/timed.rst:19-22 #d4b5b9f5fa22
#c54[i4] ItsDangerous provides URL-safe serializers for passing trusted strings where only a limited character set is available.
  > docs/url_safe.rst:7-8 #89cc291f0098
#c55[i4] URLSafeSerializer can be imported from itsdangerous.url_safe to serialize and deserialize data with a secret key.
  > docs/url_safe.rst:12 #f1c40a2fe73b
#c56[i3] The itsdangerous.url_safe module provides the URLSafeTimedSerializer class.
  > docs/url_safe.rst:21 #a08f23eb5918

## src/itsdangerous
#c57[i3] The itsdangerous package exposes base64_decode, base64_encode, and want_bytes from its encoding module.
  > src/itsdangerous/__init__.py:1-3 #164d39b0e85e
#c58[i4] The package exposes exception classes BadData, BadHeader, BadPayload, BadSignature, BadTimeSignature, and SignatureExpired from its exc module.
  > src/itsdangerous/__init__.py:4-9 #9fd05afd1421
#c59[i4] The package re-exports Serializer from serializer, and HMACAlgorithm, NoneAlgorithm, and Signer from signer.
  > src/itsdangerous/__init__.py:10-13 #1adafc6dc096
#c60[i4] TimedSerializer and TimestampSigner are imported and re-exported from the timed module.
  > src/itsdangerous/__init__.py:14-15 #b0f048ff2731
#c61[i4] URLSafeSerializer and URLSafeTimedSerializer are imported and re-exported from the url_safe module.
  > src/itsdangerous/__init__.py:16-17 #7f3d64f8272a
#c62[i3] _CompactJSON wraps the json module to strip whitespace when serializing JSON data.
  > src/itsdangerous/_json.py::_CompactJSON #9510131aae41
#c63[i4] _CompactJSON.loads deserializes a str or bytes payload using json.loads.
  > src/itsdangerous/_json.py::_CompactJSON.loads #ff9e48a0e634
#c64[i5] _CompactJSON.dumps defaults ensure_ascii to False and separators to (',', ':') before delegating to json.dumps.
  > src/itsdangerous/_json.py::_CompactJSON.dumps #afad4d46d4aa
#c65[i5] base64_encode converts input to bytes via want_bytes, generates URL-safe base64, and strips trailing '=' padding characters.
  > src/itsdangerous/encoding.py::base64_encode #afcca8ea5167
#c66[i3] int_to_bytes packs an integer as a big-endian 64-bit unsigned int and strips leading null bytes.
  > src/itsdangerous/encoding.py::int_to_bytes #f8e965df86f5
#c67[i3] bytes_to_int left-pads a byte string to 8 bytes with null bytes and unpacks it as a big-endian 64-bit unsigned int.
  > src/itsdangerous/encoding.py::bytes_to_int #672e94702b08
#c68[i5] BadData inherits from Exception and serves as the base class for all exceptions defined in ItsDangerous.
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::BadData #dd4e1e9667a0
#c69[i4] BadSignature inherits from BadData and stores the payload that failed the signature verification in self.payload.
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::BadSignature.__init__ #8c23f8689345
#c70[i4] BadTimeSignature is a subclass of BadSignature that optionally records the signature creation timestamp in date_signed.
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::BadTimeSignature #20a1bf2bb0a7
#c71[i4] SignatureExpired subclasses BadTimeSignature and is raised when a signature timestamp exceeds max_age.
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::SignatureExpired #5b7d75349cb2
#c72[i3] BadHeader inherits from BadSignature and holds optional malformed header data as well as an optional original_error exception.
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::BadHeader #53ceced8b022
#c73[i4] BadPayload inherits directly from BadData and stores the underlying loading exception in original_error.
  > src/itsdangerous/exc.py::BadPayload #564bc548d3f2
#c74[i3] The secret_key property returns the newest, last item in the Serializer instance's secret_keys list.
  > src/itsdangerous/serializer.py:208 #4ef723528107
#c75[i4] Serializer.load_payload wraps unserialization errors into a BadPayload exception containing the original error.
  > src/itsdangerous/serializer.py:264-270 #cec35b6b2f4b
#c76[i3] Serializer.dump_payload always returns bytes, encoding text output from text serializers as UTF-8.
  > src/itsdangerous/serializer.py::Serializer.dump_payload #257e5945c1a3
#c77[i4] Serializer.loads_unsafe never fails, returning a (signature_valid, payload) tuple where signature_valid is a boolean indicating whether the signature was valid.
  > src/itsdangerous/serializer.py:354-358 #e045117c8bc5
#c78[i4] SigningAlgorithm.verify_signature uses hmac.compare_digest to safely compare the candidate signature against get_signature.
  > src/itsdangerous/signer.py::SigningAlgorithm.verify_signature #b4c5b21d12cf
#c79[i3] _lazy_sha1 defers importing or calling hashlib.sha1 to runtime so FIPS builds without SHA-1 do not fail on import.
  > src/itsdangerous/signer.py::_lazy_sha1 #63568e118815
#c80[i4] Signer rejects separator characters present in _base64_alphabet to ensure the separator cannot appear in the signature itself.
  > src/itsdangerous/signer.py:146-151 #00bb91caa000
#c81[i4] Signer uses the newest secret key, located at the end of secret_keys, when signing and when deriving keys without an explicit key.
  > src/itsdangerous/signer.py:139 #631f9f46207d
#c82[i4] derive_key supports 'concat', 'django-concat', 'hmac', and 'none', raising TypeError for unrecognized derivation methods.
  > src/itsdangerous/signer.py::Signer.derive_key #2806bf6119c7
#c83[i4] Signer.get_signature encodes algorithm-generated signatures with base64_encode after deriving the key.
  > src/itsdangerous/signer.py::Signer.get_signature #5f8eadd2fbc7
#c84[i2] TimestampSigner.get_timestamp returns the current time as an integer using int(time.time()).
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py::TimestampSigner.get_timestamp #de77c2431b9b
#c85[i3] TimestampSigner.timestamp_to_datetime converts an integer timestamp into a UTC timezone-aware datetime instance.
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py::TimestampSigner.timestamp_to_datetime #2241fa332731
#c86[i4] TimestampSigner.sign encodes the integer timestamp as base64 and appends it between the payload value and signature using sep.
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py::TimestampSigner.sign #58138f9920de
#c87[i3] TimestampSigner.unsign raises BadTimeSignature if the separator is missing or the timestamp bytes cannot be decoded.
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py:106 #7bbf3cb843b4
#c88[i3] TimestampSigner.validate returns True if unsigning succeeds, catching BadSignature and returning False otherwise.
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py::TimestampSigner.validate #b483961f1082
#c89[i4] TimedSerializer.loads iterates through unsigners and immediately re-raises SignatureExpired without attempting subsequent signers.
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py::TimedSerializer #7aae72ea6cd9
#c90[i3] TimedSerializer uses TimestampSigner as its default_signer class.
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py::TimedSerializer #7aae72ea6cd9
#c91[i3] URLSafeSerializerMixin uses _CompactJSON as its default_serializer.
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializerMixin #1b2723627ade
#c92[i4] In URLSafeSerializerMixin.dump_payload, payloads are zlib-compressed only if the compressed length is strictly less than len(json) - 1.
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializerMixin.dump_payload #337cc17a522e
#c93[i4] When URLSafeSerializerMixin dumps compressed payload bytes, it prefixes the base64-encoded output with b'.'.
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializerMixin.dump_payload #337cc17a522e
#c94[i4] In load_payload, URLSafeSerializerMixin checks for a leading b'.' to strip it and mark the payload for zlib decompression.
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializerMixin #1b2723627ade
#c95[i3] Failure to base64-decode a payload in URLSafeSerializerMixin raises a BadPayload exception wrapping the original error.
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializerMixin #1b2723627ade
#c96[i3] Failure during zlib decompression in URLSafeSerializerMixin raises a BadPayload exception.
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializerMixin #1b2723627ade
#c97[i2] URLSafeSerializer combines URLSafeSerializerMixin and Serializer[str].
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeSerializer #f82417cd241a
#c98[i2] URLSafeTimedSerializer combines URLSafeSerializerMixin and TimedSerializer[str].
  > src/itsdangerous/url_safe.py::URLSafeTimedSerializer #2ef0e70571b8
#c99[i5] In itsdangerous.serializer, is_text_serializer checks whether a given data serializer generates text or binary output by testing if serializer.dumps({}) returns a str.
  > src/itsdangerous/serializer.py:33-37 #35d089511225
#c100[i3] TimestampSigner.unsign returns a tuple of the value and decoded datetime when return_timestamp is True.
  > src/itsdangerous/timed.py:155-156 #9a3eaf098eac

